  "question": {
    "text": "Let the circumcentre of <math><mo>∆</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>S</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and the midpoints of the sides <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> and <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> are <math><mi>E</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>F</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively, then the coordinates of <math><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;are"
